id: pm-slack-loss-aware-payloads
title: Compile bounded Slack payloads with exact loss receipts
description: "Compile Slack wire payloads with per-field clipping and omission receipts plus stable recovery links. Scope excludes generic redaction, output budgeting and renderer registries."
type: Feature
status: closed
priority: 2
tags[3]: loss-receipts,payload,slack
created_at: "2026-10-29T05:49:43.965Z"
updated_at: "2026-10-30T20:35:46.689Z"
closed_at: "2026-10-30T20:35:44.907Z"
completed_at: "2026-10-29T10:15:38.000Z"
author: codex-agent
acceptance_criteria: Oversized block and text fixtures respect documented payload bounds; Every clipped source span is accounted for with a recovery link; Urgent status and identity fields are never silently removed; Malformed payloads refuse before sending
release: 2026.10.30
resolution: "Delivered by PR #171 (2b681db): Compile bounded Slack messages with exact loss receipts"
expected_result: Oversized block and text fixtures respect documented payload bounds; Every clipped source span is accounted for with a recovery link; Urgent status and identity fields are never silently removed; Malformed payloads refuse before sending
actual_result: "PR #171 merged at 2026-10-29T10:15:38Z as 2b681db; required CI passed on the merged head."
comments[15]{created_at,author,text}:
  "2026-10-29T05:50:04.404Z",codex-agent,"Overlap recheck: core output budgets govern JSON/TOON projection, existing attention coalescing governs event counts, and pm-slack-standup owns standup generation. Existing Slack renderers truncate fields without receipts. No equivalent compiler or duplicate open item/PR found. Design: a pure bounded compiler and strict shared wire schema; explicit protected paths and stable recovery URLs; SDK-backed read-only item projection; no new durable state, leases, import, sync, or remote writes. Existing delivery state machines remain separate. No transaction isolation claim: commitWorkspaceTransaction does not exclude ordinary writers (pm-cli#1620). Read-only compilation observes a snapshot and never applies a saved plan."
  "2026-10-29T06:00:56.256Z",codex-agent,"Implementation: shared strict static Block Kit schema validates compiler inputs and every outbound webhook payload; pure compiler records nonoverlapping original UTF-16 ranges, typed protected_overflow refusals and recovery links. SDK item projection protects identity, status, priority, assignee, parent and full dependency fields without lifecycle name comparisons. Canonical full SDK reads explicitly disable output budgets; command uses only the host-injected client. Compact paginated TOON/JSON output carries a source digest. Focused oversized/schema/zero-socket tests pass; seeded 500-sequence no-git readback and packed acceptance are underway."
  "2026-10-29T06:04:22.308Z",codex-agent,"Public read-only validation at main d01c295bb719b74df06d075b4df9d6719cfd3cda: 96 items compiled, 0 refusals, 1 exact text clipping receipt, 0 omissions, 95944 total payload bytes, maximum 3312 bytes and 4 blocks, 96 identical replays. All 199 copied tracker files and permissions unchanged; git absent from PATH; 0 mutations/posts. Reproduction and measured scope are recorded in docs/payload-compilation-validation.md."
  "2026-10-29T06:20:10.658Z",codex-agent,"Verification: linked node --test --test-concurrency=2 test/payload-compilation.test.ts passed 7 tests including 500 seeded SDK readback/replay sequences. Additional focused boundary tests cover full-read refusals, strict envelope byte caps and regular-file input. Behavioral revert proof passed: pass-through compiler fails, removing the pre-send guard fails, restoring both passes. Packed acceptance passed all five supported installation shapes on pm 2026.10.28; CI now repeats the captured-artifact acceptance on Node 26. Full npm/Bun release gates remain CI evidence, not a local full-suite claim. Local health has inherited global pm-github host-version skew plus the already-tracked legacy provenance advisory; neither was repaired or rewritten."
  "2026-10-29T06:29:24.302Z",codex-agent,"Final boundary review found that shared-reference SDK input could describe an oversized JSON expansion. Added cumulative encoded-string accounting during the same strict parse, before aggregate serialization; a dense fixture describes roughly 2.5 GB through shared references and refuses promptly. The final exact envelope/wire checks remain in place. Six focused compiler/transport/source tests pass after the hardening. Earlier CI already passed both npm gates and entered Bun gates; the follow-up push requires fresh exact-head evidence."
  "2026-10-29T06:37:54.743Z",codex-agent,"Implementation head 57f1e2a passed https://github.com/unbraind/pm-slack/actions/runs/40829578310: npm and Bun release gates on Node 22 and 26, each 1012/1012 tests with 100 percent lines, branches and functions (4048 gate test executions total). Captured-artifact acceptance passed 5/5 install shapes; SHA-256 0852eaee3ba60eab940b63a6637a5c0d483a356447d41d67fab438868447ff87. CodeQL passed. The final-source public read-only probe again matched all recorded numbers: 96 items, 1 clipping receipt, max 3312 bytes/4 blocks, 199 unchanged files, 96 exact replays, zero mutations/posts. PR: https://github.com/unbraind/pm-slack/pull/171 (ready for review). Bot review availability is missing evidence: CodeRabbit skipped automatic review, Greptile expired, Cubic neutral. This receipt commit needs a fresh CI run before final handoff; no item closure, merge or release."
  "2026-10-29T06:44:13.978Z",codex-agent,"API review: keep the native snapshot adapter internal instead of exporting it from the package entry point. A real SDK fields projection can retain body while omitting lifecycle/relationship fields, so only compileSlackItem(client, id, link) owns and guarantees the full read. Public compiler/validator APIs are unchanged otherwise. The internal adapter remains directly testable for budget and projected-source refusals. Typecheck, test typing, docstrings, build and two focused API/command tests passed; a fresh exact-head gate follows this API-only narrowing."
  "2026-10-29T06:54:01.589Z",codex-agent,"CI cutoff handoff: stopped polling after the prescribed 30-minute wait. API head 90733df2feaf113d1eff6f537e136bf3549cfc6f is in https://github.com/unbraind/pm-slack/actions/runs/40831124586. Node 26 completed successfully (npm and Bun release gates plus 5-install artifact acceptance). Node 22 completed npm and was still running the Bun release gate at cutoff. CodeQL passed: https://github.com/unbraind/pm-slack/actions/runs/40831124559. Earlier implementation and evidence heads passed all four gates at 1012 tests each and unchanged 100-percent coverage thresholds. Final API and this evidence-only receipt still require exact-head CI confirmation by the orchestrator; pending checks are not approval. PR https://github.com/unbraind/pm-slack/pull/171 remains ready for review; item remains in_progress with own claim released. No merge or release."
  "2026-10-29T07:18:37.274Z",codex-agent,"Re-review resumed on clean branch; origin/main is already an ancestor (0 commits behind), so no merge is required. Blocking classes: bounded untrusted input must also have bounded compilation work (avoid repeated global scans/serialization); archive handling must never follow links while changing permissions or cleaning copies. Auditing all compiler passes, output producers, packed consumers, archive probes and permission writers. GitHub contains no additional inline findings; checking the orchestrator report for any non-blocking items before declaring the review addressed."
  "2026-10-29T08:03:47.063Z",codex-agent,"R1 class audit completed. Bounded-work rule: replaced all three global source-leaf rescan sites with one pass/indexed counts; replaced repeated block filtering/JSON serialization with exact per-block byte accounting. JSON/TOON, SDK, offline CLI and all five packed consumers share the compiler and adversarial corpus (up to 500 blocks/50000 fields), with exact callback and serialization-volume budgets. Mutation-ownership rule: both archive probes now preflight before chmod and share no-follow inode-bound permissions and directory-only cleanup. Outbox constructor/migration writers also reject linked parents/files/sidecars; old read-only stores remain readable without new chmod/validation. Added real link/hardlink/special-file/replaced-inode tests, a linked Git archive and peer mkdir/mode interleavings. Revert proof: restoring global leaf rescans FAILS; restoring repeated payload serialization FAILS; restoring old archive traversal FAILS; unchecked pathname chmod FAILS; restored implementation PASSES. No additional non-blocking finding text was supplied or present in GitHub; no supplied finding was dismissed. Full npm/Bun gates now run serially with two workers."
  "2026-10-29T08:48:56.733Z",codex-agent,"R1 full npm run release:check passed locally in a credential-free isolated home with two test workers: 1019 tests passed, zero failures/skips, 100 percent lines/branches/functions across all nine runtime sources. Auditing, packed contents, changelog and release-attestation/date checks also passed. Instrumented 200-section/20000-field input: 586112 input bytes, 42709 callback visits, 1917870 encoded bytes, 1880 ms; 500-section/50000-field input: 1465112 input bytes, 104209 callback visits, 4743270 encoded bytes, 2605 ms. Exact callback/serialization budgets are the regression oracle; timing is display evidence. The full Bun gate is running serially next, followed by native Bun and all five packed consumers."
  "2026-10-29T09:13:21.258Z",codex-agent,"R1 full bun run release:check also passed locally: 1019 tests passed, zero failures/skips, all nine runtime sources at 100 percent lines/branches/functions with unchanged thresholds and two workers. Coverage duration was 2356230 ms on the shared host; all remaining release checks passed. Native Bun acceptance passed real no-git SDK/CLI/outbox/migration scenarios, including stale-peer preservation and five read-only lifecycle modes. The single-artifact five-install acceptance is running next; the public read-only snapshot is being remeasured with the fixed archive helper."
  "2026-10-29T09:15:05.665Z",codex-agent,"Final-source public validation with the safe archive helper matched all previous numbers: public main d01c295bb719b74df06d075b4df9d6719cfd3cda, 96/96 items compiled, zero refusals, one clipping receipt, zero whole omissions, 95944 total bytes, maximum 3312 bytes/4 blocks, 96 identical replays, all 199 copied files and permissions unchanged, zero mutations/posts, git absent from PATH. Fresh origin/main check remains 0 commits behind; no merge required. Full gate and acceptance commands are linked as item tests; the linked adversarial revert command was run through pm test with progress and passed."
  "2026-10-29T09:19:02.940Z",codex-agent,"R1 captured-artifact acceptance passed 5/5 supported install shapes: project-local, npm global, Bun global, npx and bunx on pm 2026.10.28. Each repeats five exact bounded-work shapes, ten real linked-storage cases, dense 20000-field CLI JSON/TOON, SDK reads and loss pagination; zero Slack posts. Captured tarball SHA-256 394415fe5ee2210ac443b531f19828dfcc31415c5caa9a45b7337637f7a7f7eb. Both full local gates passed 1019 tests each and 100 percent runtime coverage; four behavioral mutants fail and fixed tests pass. Both reported classes are addressed throughout package-owned paths. Remaining limitation: checked descriptors guard permission targets, but SQLite still has the documented path-check/open window against concurrent hierarchy replacement. No further non-blocking findings were supplied; no finding was dismissed. Releasing own claim for exact-head CI and orchestrator re-review; never merge or release."
  "2026-10-29T09:51:48.049Z",codex-agent,"R1 CI cutoff handoff after the prescribed 30-minute wait: runtime head c7a3f005512200a24b9562c9a4df404005d5b4a6 is in https://github.com/unbraind/pm-slack/actions/runs/40848982092. Node 26 passed both full npm/Bun release gates and 5/5 captured installs. Node 22 was running npm with Bun still pending; CodeQL passed at https://github.com/unbraind/pm-slack/actions/runs/40848982013. Pending checks are not approval. Both local gates passed 1019 tests each with 100 percent lines/branches/functions. This final evidence-only receipt requires fresh exact-head CI confirmation; check https://github.com/unbraind/pm-slack/pull/171/checks before merge. PR remains ready for review; both reported classes and all supplied findings are fixed, own claim remains released, no merge or release. Stopping polling at the required cutoff."
